---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, pathFor } from '../../config/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy choices and deletion" description="How to remove Golden Moments family-photo copies, delete local app data, manage backups, and ask about support records.">
  <section class="interior-hero">
    <div class="reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Golden Moments / Privacy</p>
      <h1>Your privacy choices</h1>
      <p class="interior-lede">Your photos belong to you. These steps explain the controls available on your device and how to contact us about information you have sent to support.</p>
      <p class="small-print">Updated October 18, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="reading-column prose-page">
    <h2>Remove one imported photo</h2>
    <p>If the personal-photo feature is available in your installed app version, open <strong>Your family photos</strong>, find the selected image, and choose <strong>Remove</strong>. Confirm the action. This removes the working copy held by Golden Moments, not the original photograph in Apple's Photos library.</p>
    <h2>Remove all imported-photo copies</h2>
    <p>Open <strong>Your family photos → Remove all photo copies</strong> and confirm. The app will remove its local collection. If an error occurs, try again and contact support rather than deleting originals from your Photos library.</p>
    <h2>Remove the app's remaining data</h2>
    <p>On an iPhone or iPad, use the device's <strong>Delete App</strong> option and follow the system's prompts. <strong>Offload App</strong> is different: it can keep documents and data. We cannot remove files from a device you control by sending an email request because Golden Moments does not operate a remote account or photo server.</p>
    <h2>Check backups and other copies</h2>
    <p>Deleting app copies does not guarantee deletion from previously created iCloud, computer, or other backups. Review backup settings and retention through the relevant Apple or device controls. Copies shared through other applications or kept on a different device must be handled separately.</p>
    <h2>Choose what you send to support</h2>
    <p>Our support channel is email, not an in-app upload service. Sending a support request tells us your email address and whatever information you include. Please avoid sending photographs, diagnoses, patient records, or other sensitive details when a short technical description will do.</p>
    <h2>Request access or deletion of information held by us</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL + '?subject=Golden%20Moments%20privacy%20request'}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> to ask about or request deletion of support correspondence or other personal information we may hold. We will handle requests under applicable law and may need limited information to establish authorization. We cannot delete content stored only on your phone or controlled by an independent provider.</p>
    <h2>Optional permissions</h2>
    <p>Photo import is optional. You can decline to choose photographs and still enjoy built-in pictures. Your system's Photos permissions, where applicable, are managed in the device's Settings. Revoking photo access does not necessarily erase copies you already imported into the app; remove those through the controls above.</p>
    <p>Read our <a href={pathFor('/app-privacy/')}>mobile app privacy policy</a> for more details, or the <a href={pathFor('/privacy/')}>website privacy notice</a> for site-specific information.</p>
    <p class="back-home"><a class="text-link" href={pathFor('/legal/')}>← Legal information</a></p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
